# Student Performance Prediction Using Machine Learning

## Project Overview

This project analyzes student performance data and applies machine
learning techniques to predict mathematics scores.

## Objectives

- Perform exploratory data analysis
- Handle missing values
- Remove duplicate records
- Encode categorical variables
- Prepare data for machine learning
- Train multiple machine learning models
- Evaluate model performance
- Compare different models

## Machine Learning Models

1. Linear Regression
2. Random Forest Regression

## Evaluation Metrics

- Mean Absolute Error (MAE)
- Root Mean Squared Error (RMSE)
- R² Score

## Technologies Used

- Python
- Pandas
- NumPy
- Matplotlib
- Seaborn
- Scikit-learn
- Jupyter Notebook

## Dataset

Student Performance Dataset containing demographic information,
parental education, test preparation information, and student scores.

## Results

The models are compared using MAE, RMSE, and R² Score.
The model with lower prediction errors and higher R² Score
provides better performance on the test dataset.

## Conclusion

The project demonstrates the complete machine learning workflow,
from data preprocessing and exploratory analysis to model training,
evaluation, and comparison.